      4 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">اشأم</span></b>  <i>He desired the left:</i> like as <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَيْمَنَ</span> signifies “ he desired the right. ” (TA in art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">يمن</span>.)
― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  And <i>He</i> (a man, S) <i>came to</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">الشَّأْم</span> [i. e. <i>Syria</i>]:
(S, K, TA: [see also 3:]) or <i>he went thither:</i>
and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَيْمَنَ</span> signifies “ he came to El-Yemen. ”
(TA.) ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَا أَشْأَمَهُ</span> (S, K, TA) <i>How unlucky,</i> or
<i>inauspicious, is he!</i> (TA:) the vulgar say, <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَا</span>
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَيْشَمَهُ</span>. (S, TA.)

